"""Negative detector for quote, code and separator tokens.

Layer 0, MLP neuron-like component (down_proj:3577). It is almost never positive. It goes
strongly negative on tokens that open or close a quoted or marked-up span: the chat end
marker, Japanese corner brackets, backticks for inline code, guillemets, and long rules
made of one repeated symbol. Everything else is about zero. The program writes a fixed
negative value for each kind.
